From: Thien An Dang Thanh <24854119+thienandangthanh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:15:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Send DC PSCell Change control with an en-gNB-UEID

rc now sends only CONTROL Service Style 5 "Dual Connectivity control",
Control Action ID 3 "DC PSCell Change control" (E2SM-RC v03.00 7.6.6.1),
the control a source en-gNB executes as an SN-initiated SN change. The RIC
Control Header Format 1 carries UE ID en-gNB-UEID {m-eNB-UE-X2AP-ID,
globalENB-ID {pLMN-Identity, macro eNB ID}} with no optional member; the
gNB-UEID header path is removed. The message keeps RAN parameters
1 > 2 > 3 > 4 with the APER NR CGI (8.4.6.3).

The gRPC UeId gains enGNBUEID {mEnbUeX2apId, globalEnbPlmn,
globalEnbMacroId} as field 2; rc.pb.go is regenerated with the pinned
protoc 3.6.1 toolchain. The service validates every request through the
nil-safe getters and refuses with InvalidArgument, sending nothing, when
EnGnbUEID is absent, when GnbUEID is also set, when a member is out of
range or malformed, or when the style/action is not 5/3. A unit test
covers the admitted forms and each refusal.
